## Installation

1. Download `{{MODULE_ID}}-{{VERSION}}.zip` from
   [Releases](https://github.com/{{REPO}}/releases).
2. Flash the zip in Magisk, KernelSU, or APatch.
3. Reboot your device.

## Build from source

```bash
./build.sh
```

The flashable zip is written to `dist/{{MODULE_ID}}-{{VERSION}}.zip`.
Build output and release zips are intentionally ignored by git.

## Release flow

1. Bump `version` and `versionCode` in `module.prop`.
2. Add a `## [{{VERSION}}]` section to `CHANGELOG.md`.
3. Commit and push.
4. Tag the same version and push the tag:

   ```bash
   git tag {{VERSION}}
   git push origin main --tags
   ```

The release workflow validates the tag against `module.prop`, builds the zip,
publishes the GitHub release, and refreshes `update.json` on `{{BRANCH}}`.

## Project layout

```text
.
├── module.prop          # module identity and OTA endpoint
├── customize.sh         # installer logic (SKIPUNZIP + permissions)
├── service.sh           # late_start service hook
├── action.sh            # root-manager action button
├── uninstall.sh         # cleanup on removal
├── system/              # systemless overlay payload
├── webroot/             # optional WebUI payload
├── build.sh             # reproducible module zip builder
├── update.json          # OTA manifest consumed by root managers
└── .github/workflows/   # build + release automation
```

